    "created_at": "2016-07-18T14:39:39Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-07-18T14:39:46Z",
    "body": "> The specification is quite clear in that it shouldn't bubble.\n\nYep, it certainly is, and it's not at all surprising to me that Chrome implemented it to-spec.\n\nAs a developer, I do think it would make sense and be more useful for this event to bubble so delegated event handlers can be used. There _are_ ways around this in lieu of this event not bubbling, but it would make much more sense to me if the event bubbled.\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
